      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those sudden crashes are often a classic sign of high blood sugar spikes followed by an aggressive insulin drop, even if your levels seem normal in the morning. To investigate, try tracking tightly timed blood glucose readings alongside your meals, or consult a doctor for tests like HbA1c to rule out undiagnosed issues like prediabetes or reactive hypoglycemia. If you consistently avoid high-GI breakfasts and avoid using this meal approach most people try to improve energy stability, those spikes and crashes may be your body's warning to slow down the carb absorption before it happens.",
